{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LANDED & CLOSED. Gerrit change 2423 (Change-Id I2bfedd80858926b8289f9d798e6223199ded6465), patchset 2, merged as main commit `0b8ef3b7592800bf636609444d510639fbfee799`.\n\nVotes at submit: LLM-Review +1 (PASS, clean) AND Verified +1 (CI run 33300320778, SUCCESS); unresolved comments 0. Submitted (Rebase-If-Necessary rebased server-side). Closed with close_class=preexisting (no --caused-by: the reported behavior was already made correct by merged change 2345 / d240 before this ticket's work; there is no single introducing commit for a defect that did not reproduce at verification).\n\nWhat landed (non-behavioral regression-guard, per the re-scope):\n- AC#3 fail-loud guard: `instrument_certified_tools` now raises RuntimeError if it ever meets a certified tool already `is_async` at instrument time (impossible under the load-bearing instrument-first/offload-second order in `wire_health`). Converts silent fail-open into a loud failure a test catches. RED-first: new test `test_instrument_certified_tools_fails_loud_on_an_already_async_certified_tool` (verified RED \"DID NOT RAISE\" before the guard; GREEN after; mutation-checked by reverting the guard → RED). Updated `test_certified_tool_instrumentation_moves_the_gauge` to drop the now-outlawed silent-skip assertion, and refreshed stale \"skips tools already marked async\" cross-references in `offload_sync_tools`/`wire_health` docstrings.\n- AC#1 property pinned by existing/observable regression tests (cited in the RCA comment): off-loop execution (`tests/unit/test_mcp_tool_offload.py`), SIGTERM serviced + gauge drains (`test_make_sigterm_handler_stops_intake_then_drains`), bounded drain honoring grace_seconds/deadline in both drains-in-time and never-drains-within-grace cases (`test_drain_then_exit_*`).\n- AC#2 docs: `docs/adr/0104-mcp-on-box.md` and `docs/adr/0079-autodeploy-on-box-timer.md` now state the real threading model — sync tool body offloaded to an anyio worker via `offload_sync_tools`; the drain contract holds because of that offload + bounded grace.\n\nGates green pre-push: make lint, make typecheck; targeted MCP tests pass; module-size gate passes (`_mcp_health.py` kept ≤800 LOC). No product behavior change; guard is inert in the production instrument-first/offload-second order and only fires on a future misconfiguration."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788078405905820189,"uuid":"d36c49c4-4aa2-4a8c-9204-a4903dbaf182"}